WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
In first aid, shock isn't just about being surprised.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.900
Shock is a critical life-threatening state where the body isn't getting the blood flow

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.760
and oxygen it needs.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.400
If nothing is done, shock can lead to vital organ failure and death.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.480
It can be triggered by severe bleeding, serious infections, heart failure, or even a major

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:23.020
allergic reaction or spinal injury.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.559
As an everyday hero, you need to be able to spot the signs of shock quickly.

00:00:27.559 --> 00:00:33.740
The person might feel weak, dizzy, or lightheaded, and their skin often becomes cool, pale, and

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:34.799
clammy.

00:00:34.799 --> 00:00:39.720
You might also notice they seem confused, have a weak but rapid pulse, or are taking

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.139
very rapid, shallow breaths.

00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:46.980
If you suspect someone is going into shock, your first move is to call 911.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.520
While you wait for professional help, have the person lie down flat on their back.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.419
If they aren't having any trouble breathing, you can prop their feet up about 12 inches

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.500
to help blood flow back toward their heart and brain.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.340
Because people in shock have trouble maintaining their body temperature, cover them with a

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.139
blanket to keep them warm and calm.

00:01:05.139 --> 00:01:09.739
Your final tasks are to ensure any obvious external bleeding is controlled with direct

00:01:09.739 --> 00:01:12.739
pressure and to stay right by their side.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.980
Monitor their breathing and responsiveness closely.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:21.139
If they ever stop responding and stop breathing normally, you must be ready to start CPR

00:01:21.139 --> 00:01:22.019
immediately.

